{"title":"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Clever_Construction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Clever Construction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Trig)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Mass_points_and_Ptolemy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Mass points and Ptolemy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is drawn such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab757085426e6962c7d3068e5180cccf07a5cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5322c7f896502c208bbb4a354efc8d212620667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0938b1cb2a92765e576c16687c904efdf2cb03a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is a square that contains vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in its interior. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/2627704555ddbedd1cc325a93f80bbe8760f8e36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2+CF^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Clever_Construction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Clever_Construction)\">Solution 1 (Clever Construction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Clever Construction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Invites12.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Invites12.png/300px-Invites12.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"304\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Invites12.png/450px-Invites12.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/1e/Invites12.png/600px-Invites12.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We draw a line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17630e2de0e73454e7238072684ab9b2da2f3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG \\perp CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. We then draw a line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6ad1ae9ee96d4a8173251c88df88a30efb25ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH \\perp EG$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />. Finally, we extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffb105232a8a0e6307866e5d52ccb9e6db45c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0d0e8f05ddf458a65ac8bc93b1919fdf9f8bb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI \\perp FH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Next, if we mark <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10a2dee30b7c2a0575d69397aea2b1c6b17c985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f14ed20e73636341550146921c1da1ca299f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDC = 90-x$\" width=\"132\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97d7a3450ee8c1c38ee2179da90fedb2ada34a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EDG = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />. We repeat this, finding  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db8fe83f75ea3662de8bcb37c76ffda994fb1c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBD = \\angle EDG = \\angle FEH = \\angle BFI = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"333\" height=\"14\" />, so by AAS congruence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f7c823ce2dbf565bb3306452e6abdcdce0d687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDC \\cong \\triangle DEG \\cong \\triangle EFH \\cong \\triangle FBI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"18\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf14d5fe54bfc4197f2f4ab5f9e2ee8bcac0ee4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = DG = EH = FI = AD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"275\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee1da34dbcc331b9307f4edb797c66b31e40709.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC = EG = FH = BI = AB = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"274\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c5a21009bb712942a8ae31b9434dd173f1cc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CG = GH = HI = IC = 7-4 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"282\" height=\"16\" />. We see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcbcc59d24b8f9a9755b9bed5f9a21c724db36a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF^2 = CI^2 + IF^2 = 3^2 + 4^2 = 9 + 16 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/7835e768c2836b639a7aeba406eb377f3b8504aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2 = CG^2 + GE^2 = 3^2 + 7^2 = 9 + 49 = 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"352\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d373fb2a6f0c48805c632e1edeb77993de069813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF^2 + CE^2 = 25 + 58 = \\boxed{83}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"238\" height=\"25\" /> ~Bradygho\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Trig)\">Solution 2 (Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a02d10609ca7148bd488e0925e2a0d50dc1660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBC = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895fb2440c3ad71e6b1073d39df13ea882f64b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(90- \\theta)=\\sin(\\theta)=\\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"230\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75063bffec2321e5c6ef022e60f7f2aac11c2023.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle CDE)=\\frac{4 \\sqrt{65}}{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"43\" />. Now, Law Of cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5425baeec765203a664dc6bd0f0562f2bf485a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acd42ef30a6319e5b63f48ae3e8a11120e56f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCF$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d5eb5fa5326a70349b1d816dd2720d757a242e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF^2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/0732e06696b0dd70de141b5d88f9510f6e3c70b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2=58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c075b67ed76e11be441500084e7ca1b338b612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE^2+CF^2=\\boxed{83}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"155\" height=\"25\" /> ~ Geometry285\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Mass_points_and_Ptolemy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Mass_points_and_Ptolemy)\">Solution 3 (Mass points and Ptolemy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Mass points and Ptolemy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0938b1cb2a92765e576c16687c904efdf2cb03a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDEF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />.  Applying moment of inertia to the system of mass points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/7264241986437c3e13df27da2024b86a5e64442e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Sigma = {1B,1D,1E,1F}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> (which has center of mass <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cdc60aa1a90f2f2ac9bf3263ce58419e892fe5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CB^2 + CD^2 + CE^2 + CF^2 = OB^2 + OD^2 + OE^2 + OF^2 + 4OC^2.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"17\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86644a0d74ba9ba18fc2e69713901863ab6c3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle, we may further cancel out some terms via Pythag to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d005024d3b13d120d99ab2648b5d64846ee9f2ed.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CE^2 + CF^2 = OE^2 + OF^2 + 4OC^2 = 65 + 4OC^2.\\]\" width=\"393\" height=\"17\" /> To compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8f2f1a3ddc6b42fae25a0637e85c747875180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, apply Ptolemy to cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/3455c5f6b4a41df62efa14d200d4ab76ee724523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DOCB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> (using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/2243d7f1d5750ddbe47c7dc0eca42e593d9f5f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is 45-45-90) to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181d41a80daeeb269ca439cb1f4dc8445316afee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OC = \\tfrac{3}{\\sqrt 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" />.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1bc5e22a67fa944bb624ac86e7613076efa4c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CE^2 + CF^2 = 65 + 4\\cdot\\frac 92 = 65 + 18 = \\boxed{83}.\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"37\" /> ~djmathman\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017020107\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.066 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 268/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8985/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.386      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    8.386      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21640:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017020107 and revision id 168326. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}